  "history_summaries": [
    "Fixed clearBit bug (good_bakery.scala lines 55-57): bitmask literals \"b001\".U, \"b010\".U, \"b100\".U lacked explicit width, so Chisel created 1-bit, 2-bit, 3-bit masks respectively. ~1'b1 = 1'b0 extended to 3'b000 (clears all bits); ~2'b10 = 2'b01 extended to 3'b001 (clears bits 1+2). Added explicit width (in.getWidth.W) to each literal so masks are properly sized: ~3'b001=3'b110, ~3'b010=3'b101, ~3'b100=3'b011, each clearing only the intended bit. This corruption of defer registers during L10 exit broke the ordering priority, causing two processes to enter CS simultaneously (violating MutualExclusion) and also causing spurious DetTransition failures. All 19 failing properties (MutualExclusion + all DetTransition) share this single root cause.",
    "Round 2 (assertion_error fix): Replaced all 18 buggy assertImpliesDelay(...) calls (6 transitions × 3 processes) with correct assertImpliesDelayFix(...) helper. Root cause: assertImpliesDelay uses when(delayed_ant){fvAssert(consequent)} — Chisel when blocks cannot gate concurrent AssertProperty declarations, so every DetTransition assertion emitted only the consequent checked unconditionally every cycle (e.g., pc_0==4'h1 for DetTransition_L1_to_L2_p0). The fix implements the delay pipeline manually (since delayedBool is private) and folds the delayed antecedent into the assertion condition: fvAssert(!delayed_ant || consequent), producing the correct implication delayed_ant |-> consequent. Preserved all original assertion labels exactly. No homologous assertions exist beyond the 18 calls already replaced."
  ],
